{
  "_readme": [
    "HAND-VERIFIED mapping from LeetCode topic tags to AICM patterns. Same editorial status as",
    "curriculum.json: this file is authored by a human, validated by the generator, and never",
    "produced by inference at build or run time (directive §9: 'Do not use an LLM to silently",
    "invent mappings during runtime').",
    "",
    "WHY A TABLE AND NOT A HEURISTIC. LeetCode's ~157 tags and the 28 AICM patterns are different",
    "classification systems built for different jobs. LeetCode tags a problem with the data",
    "structures and algorithms it touches; AICM names the technique a learner is practising. The",
    "overlap is real but partial, and the gaps run both ways — 'Cyclic Sort' and 'Two Heaps' have",
    "no LeetCode tag at all, while 'Rolling Hash' and 'Flow Network' have no AICM pattern. Both",
    "absences are recorded honestly rather than papered over.",
    "",
    "THE THREE MECHANISMS, applied in this order:",
    "  1. containerTags  — tags so broad they never identify a technique. Measured over the 2,561",
    "                      rated problems: Array appears on 1,649 of them, String on 625, Math on",
    "                      503. A tag on two-thirds of the corpus cannot tell anyone what to",
    "                      practise. These NEVER produce a mapping on their own; they may only",
    "                      appear inside a `combinations` rule.",
    "  2. combinations   — ordered, most-specific-first. This is what disambiguates the two tags",
    "                      that genuinely mean different patterns in different company: DFS/BFS",
    "                      over a tree is tree-dfs/tree-bfs, the same tag over a graph or a grid is",
    "                      graphs. First matching rule wins for the patterns it names.",
    "  3. direct         — single-tag mappings for everything else.",
    "",
    "CONFIDENCE is per pattern, not per problem:",
    "  exact     — the tag IS the pattern, or a combination that admits one reading.",
    "  strong    — the tag reliably implies the pattern, with rare exceptions.",
    "  heuristic — a defensible association that is too broad to filter on. Shown to the learner",
    "              as inferred; never satisfies a pattern filter and never feeds weakness.",
    "  unmapped  — nothing fired. A shipped, populated state, not a failure (directive §58).",
    "",
    "A record whose patterns all come from `heuristic` rules is reported as heuristic, and the UI",
    "says so. Silence beats false intelligence.",
    "",
    "NOTE ON THE 207: contest problems that are also curriculum questions do not use this table at",
    "all. They inherit the hand-verified AICM pattern and sub-pattern already authored for them in",
    "the 539, at confidence 'exact'. Tag inference is the fallback for the 2,354 problems the",
    "curriculum has never classified.",
    "",
    "Counts in comments are occurrences across the 2,561 rated problems, measured 2026-08-19."
  ],

